The milestone requires the player to both be within 5 blocks of the gold block AND be facing it (within 45 degrees). This ensures the agent has genuinely "found" the block — not just walked past it accidentally. The gold block is at relative position (6, 3, 4) from spawn, so the agent needs to walk approximately 7 blocks and look up slightly toward the elevated gold block. The sandbox preview confirmed this is achievable within 20 steps.

Based on the finalized scene from SceneDesignerAgent's third preview, I can now design the milestone rules. The gold block is at spawn-relative position (6, 3, 4) on a stone brick pillar. This is a "find" task, so per the preference order, I should use **position_near_with_facing** — the player must navigate near the gold block and be facing toward it to demonstrate they've "found" it.

```json
{
  "milestones": [
